It is sealed in an OutLayer TEE (Intel TDX), opened only by one pinned runner build, only when our NEAR registry contract calls.

Each sitting draws 10 of 28 hidden questions, reworded by a NEAR AI model, so an agent can't recognise the test.

@NEARProtocol 3/ Certificates are written on NEAR only from OutLayer's callback. 

Then anyone can order a surprise re-test from the site, no wallet needed. One fail suspends, a second in a row revokes.

